  "id": "congado_mineiro",
  "name": "Congado mineiro (Reinado do Rosário guards)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Brazilian Catholic devotion to Nossa Senhora do Rosário, São Benedito and Santa Efigênia, kept by brotherhoods and black communities across Minas Gerais, in which guards (guardas) of Congo, Moçambique, Catopé, Marujo and Candombe escort crowned kings and queens of Congo in the Reinado festival. Moçambique guards sing slow call-and-response cantos to caixas, ankle rattles (gungas) and the patangome shaker; Congo guards move faster with caixas, pandeiros and reco-reco; the Candombe, held to be the oldest, plays three sacred drums. A generic membrane-drum card stands in for the caixas, a generic shaker card for gungas and patangome, and a frame-drum card for the pandeiros.",
